      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Dataset List Semantics\n\nNative **ComfyUI list** flow for the `DATASET` type: **Dataset Split Batches** declares `OUTPUT_IS_LIST` and emits one execution's worth of zero-copy row batches; **Dataset From List** declares `INPUT_IS_LIST` and merges them back with one `torch.cat` (split -> merge reproduces the original rows exactly when `drop_last` is off).\n\nThis demo splits a 500-row synthetic table into shuffled 50-row batches, merges them back, and previews the head. **Dataset Get Item** picks a single row as a 1-sample view (flip its `index`). Swap the merge for per-batch training nodes to build epoch loops later."
      ],
      "title": "How this works"
    },
